So what are we going to do?

311
00:27:01,649 --> 00:27:02,649
それでいいんだっけ？
Is that really okay?

312
00:27:02,649 --> 00:27:06,549
頭は空回り死んでいく
Our heads spin in vain, dying out.

313
00:27:08,649 --> 00:27:09,849
ふざけるな
Don't mess with me!

314
00:27:09,849 --> 00:27:12,449
バイバイバズメロディ
Bye-bye, viral melody.

315
00:27:12,449 --> 00:27:15,449
歌えよ退化嘘ばかり
Sing! It's nothing but regression and lies.

316
00:27:15,449 --> 00:27:18,449
バケモノ幻想でも理想でもいい
Monster, whether it's an illusion or an ideal, it's fine.

317
00:27:18,449 --> 00:27:20,749
君の歌いたかったものはどうしたんだい？
What happened to the thing you wanted to sing?

318
00:27:20,749 --> 00:27:23,849
このままじゃ到底終われない
We absolutely cannot end it like this.

319
00:27:23,849 --> 00:27:26,849
欲しいのはきっとお金じゃない
What we want is surely not money.

320
00:27:26,849 --> 00:27:30,449
負けんな覚醒せよ子供たちよ
Don't lose! Wake up, children!

321
00:27:30,449 --> 00:27:32,849
君の歌いたかったものが聴きたいんだ
I want to hear the thing you wanted to sing.

322
00:27:32,849 --> 00:27:34,649
ふざけるな
Don't mess with me!

323
00:27:34,649 --> 00:27:37,449
バイバイバズメロディ
Bye-bye, viral melody.

324
00:27:37,449 --> 00:27:40,449
歌えよ退化嘘ばかり
Sing! It's nothing but regression and lies.

325
00:27:40,449 --> 00:27:43,449
バケモノ幻想でも理想でもいい
Monster, whether it's an illusion or an ideal, it's fine.

326
00:27:43,449 --> 00:27:45,749
君の歌いたかったものはどうしたんだい？
What happened to the thing you wanted to sing?

327
00:27:45,749 --> 00:27:47,249
嘘じゃないおカネや
It's not a lie, with money

328
00:27:47,249 --> 00:27:50,249
理想で満たす前に
and ideals, before we fill it all up,

329
00:27:50,249 --> 00:27:53,249
負けんな覚醒せよ子供たちよ
don't lose! Wake up, children!

330
00:27:53,249 --> 00:27:55,949
僕の歌いたかったものはどうしたんだい？
What happened to the thing I wanted to sing?

331
00:27:55,949 --> 00:27:57,849
意味はカンネー
I don't get the meaning!

332
00:27:57,849 --> 00:28:01,449
意味はカンネー
I don't get the meaning!

333
00:28:22,949 --> 00:28:24,949
意味はカンネー
I don't get the meaning!

334
00:28:34,449 --> 00:28:35,449
せーの
Ready, set...

335
00:28:35,449 --> 00:28:37,649
スバル先輩！
Subaru-senpai!

336
00:28:37,649 --> 00:28:40,649
お誕生日おめでとうございます！
Happy birthday!

337
00:28:40,649 --> 00:28:44,449
おめでとう！
Congratulations!

338
00:28:44,449 --> 00:28:47,449
何歳になったんだっけ？
How old did you turn again?

339
00:28:47,449 --> 00:28:49,449
20歳バージョン2！
20 years old, version 2!

340
00:28:49,449 --> 00:28:52,449
おおー！いいね！
Ooh! Nice!

341
00:28:52,449 --> 00:28:54,449
ありがとう！
Thank you!

342
00:28:54,449 --> 00:28:57,449
ちょっとみんなせっかく来てくれた
Wait, everyone went through all this trouble...

343
00:28:57,449 --> 00:29:01,449
おめでとう！
Congratulations!

344
00:28:59,949 --> 00:29:01,449
あんた違うでしょ
Wait, you've got it wrong!

345
00:29:01,449 --> 00:29:02,949
何番バージョン？
What version?

346
00:29:02,949 --> 00:29:05,449
今日の主役ですから、みずみには！
Because Mizumi is today's main character!

347
00:29:05,449 --> 00:29:08,449
で、ちょっとみんなに一言言ってね、去ってもらおうかなって
So, I thought I'd have everyone say a few words, and then have them leave!

348
00:29:08,449 --> 00:29:10,449
一人ずつ来なさい。ほら。
Come one by one. Come on!

349
00:29:10,449 --> 00:29:13,449
去る前にほら、一言言いに来なさい。ほら。
Before you leave, come say a quick word. Come on.

350
00:29:13,449 --> 00:29:15,449
誰から？ほら。
Who's first? Come on.

351
00:29:15,449 --> 00:29:17,449
嫌？うん。
No? Yeah...

352
00:29:17,449 --> 00:29:19,449
ママだよ。
I'm your mommy.

353
00:29:19,449 --> 00:29:22,449
おめでとう！おめでとう！
Happy birthday! Happy birthday!

354
00:29:22,449 --> 00:29:25,449
もう、ほら、ちゃんと、次、次、次。
Geez, come on, next, next, next!

355
00:29:25,449 --> 00:29:28,449
大丈夫っす。変な人いて怖かったでしょ？
It's okay. It was scary with that weird person, right?

356
00:29:28,449 --> 00:29:30,449
ママよ。
I'm your mommy.

357
00:29:30,449 --> 00:29:33,449
あ、違うよ。違う。違う。
Ah, that's wrong. Wrong. Wrong!

358
00:29:33,449 --> 00:29:35,449
おかしいよ！
This is weird!

359
00:29:39,449 --> 00:29:42,449
ちょっと待って、別に芸人のオーディションじゃなくて、芸人じゃないのよ。
Wait a second, this isn't some comedian audition! We're not comedians!

360
00:29:42,449 --> 00:29:45,449
肩叩いてたからビビった。
You were patting my shoulder, so I got startled.

361
00:29:45,449 --> 00:29:49,449
はい、これからもオリーお姉ちゃんに頼ってね。
Yes, continue to rely on big sister Ollie, okay?

362
00:29:49,449 --> 00:29:52,449
お姉ちゃんと思ってんの？本当に。
Do you really think of her as a big sister?

363
00:29:52,449 --> 00:29:55,449
おかしい！おかしい！
That's weird! That's weird!

364
00:29:55,449 --> 00:29:58,449
ほら、ちゃんと、最後に、最後に、最後に、最後に...
Come on, for the last one, last one, last one, last one...

365
00:29:58,449 --> 00:30:00,449
最後に、最後に...
For the last one, last one...

366
00:30:00,449 --> 00:30:02,449
でも、うちらの、すぐそこの仲やんか。
But we're very close friends, aren't we?

367
00:30:02,449 --> 00:30:03,949
だから、「せーの」って言ったら...
So, when I say "ready, set"...

368
00:30:03,606 --> 00:30:04,906
分かるよな？
You get it, right?

369
00:30:04,906 --> 00:30:05,706
イエス、イエス！
Yes, yes!

370
00:30:05,706 --> 00:30:06,606
分かった！
Got it!

371
00:30:06,606 --> 00:30:09,106
行くよ！せーの！スリー、ツー、ワン！
Here we go! Ready, set... Three, two, one!

372
00:30:09,106 --> 00:30:10,106
待って！
Wait!

373
00:30:10,106 --> 00:30:11,106
何で？
Why?

374
00:30:11,106 --> 00:30:13,106
スリー、ツー、ワン、じゃない！
Not "Three, two, one"!

375
00:30:13,106 --> 00:30:14,106
スリー、サイコー、だよ！
It's "Three, Saikou"!

376
00:30:14,106 --> 00:30:14,806
あ、スリー、サイコー、ね！
Ah, "Three, Saikou"!

377
00:30:14,806 --> 00:30:16,106
そう！せーの！
Yes! Ready, set...

378
00:30:16,106 --> 00:30:19,106
スリー、サイコー！
Three, Saikou!

379
00:30:19,106 --> 00:30:20,606
イェーイ！
Yay!

380
00:30:20,606 --> 00:30:23,106
ハート作って、ハート作って！
Make a heart, make a heart!

381
00:30:23,106 --> 00:30:24,106
これハート？
Is this a heart?

382
00:30:24,106 --> 00:30:26,106
ハート、ハート、そうそうそう！
Heart, heart, yes, yes, yes!

383
00:30:26,106 --> 00:30:27,106
大丈夫？
Is this okay?

384
00:30:27,106 --> 00:30:28,106
届けるよ！
Deliver it!

385
00:30:28,106 --> 00:30:29,106
ありがとう！
Thank you!

386
00:30:29,106 --> 00:30:31,106
ありがとうね、みんな！
Thank you, everyone!

387
00:30:31,106 --> 00:30:33,106
ここで、バイバーイ！
Bye-bye from here!

388
00:30:33,106 --> 00:30:34,406
コボも頑張って！
Kobo, do your best too!

389
00:30:34,406 --> 00:30:35,606
バイバイ！
Bye-bye!

390
00:30:35,606 --> 00:30:37,106
ママ、ママ良かったよ！
Mama, Mama was great!

391
00:30:37,106 --> 00:30:38,106
コボ、頑張ってね！
Kobo, do your best!

392
00:30:38,106 --> 00:30:40,106
頑張れ、頑張れ！
Do your best, do your best!

393
00:30:40,106 --> 00:30:42,606
バイバイ、バイバイ、頑張る、頑張る！
Bye-bye, bye-bye, I'll do my best!

394
00:30:42,606 --> 00:30:45,106
なんか、うるさかったな。
They were kind of noisy.

395
00:30:45,106 --> 00:30:47,106
頑張るか。
Alright, I'll do my best.

396
00:30:47,106 --> 00:30:49,106
よし。
Okay.

397
00:30:53,606 --> 00:30:57,606
くだらないアイの結末で
As the result of some trivial love,

398
00:30:57,606 --> 00:31:02,106
僕らは生まれ落ちて
we were born into this world,

399
00:31:02,106 --> 00:31:07,106
呼吸さえ強いられているけれど
and though we are even forced to breathe,

400
00:31:07,106 --> 00:31:11,106
綺麗な言葉並べて
we line up pretty words,

401
00:31:11,106 --> 00:31:15,106
醜さに蓋をして
put a lid on the ugliness,

402
00:31:15,106 --> 00:31:21,106
自分を愛せないままだな ずっと
and still remain unable to love ourselves, forever.

403
00:31:26,606 --> 00:31:31,106
くだらない嘘を吐くたび
Every time we tell a trivial lie,

404
00:31:31,106 --> 00:31:34,606
青色零れ落ちた
the color blue spills out.

405
00:31:34,606 --> 00:31:38,606
ガラスの瞳が綺麗で
Those glass-like eyes are beautiful,

406
00:31:38,606 --> 00:31:42,606
君のその瞼のように
just like your eyelids,

407
00:31:42,606 --> 00:31:46,606
優しい人になってさ
I want to become a kind person,

408
00:31:53,106 --> 00:31:57,606
私の呼吸に終わりがあること
That my breath will one day come to an end,

409
00:31:57,606 --> 00:32:03,106
君の声は覚えている
your voice remembers.

410
00:32:03,106 --> 00:32:07,606
生まれては消えてゆくこと
Being born and fading away,

411
00:32:07,606 --> 00:32:11,606
それだけを繰り返している
that is all we keep repeating.

412
00:32:11,606 --> 00:32:18,106
僕らがもし また会えたらなんて 思ってた
I wondered if we could ever meet again.

413
00:32:18,106 --> 00:32:23,106
生まれては消えてゆくだけの
Just being born and fading away,

414
00:32:23,106 --> 00:32:27,606
青ずんだ波に名前をつけることに
did it make any sense to give names to these blue-bruised waves,

415
00:32:27,606 --> 00:32:32,606
意味はなかったのかななんてさ
or was there no meaning after all?

416
00:32:44,106 --> 00:32:48,606
他愛ない話が染みた
Our trivial conversations soaked in,

417
00:32:48,606 --> 00:32:52,106
積み木で遊んでいる
playing with building blocks,

418
00:32:52,106 --> 00:32:56,106
崩れるその日を待ってる
waiting for the day they collapse.

419
00:32:56,106 --> 00:33:00,106
澄み切った夜の水際
At the water's edge on a clear night,

420
00:33:00,106 --> 00:33:04,106
君の頬の明るさで
the brightness of your cheeks,

421
00:33:04,106 --> 00:33:09,106
まもなく薄桜が咲くんだろう
soon, pale cherry blossoms will bloom.

422
00:33:09,106 --> 00:33:14,106
僕らの呼吸に意味がなくても
Even if our breathing has no meaning,

423
00:33:14,106 --> 00:33:19,106
二人はまた恋をする
the two of us will fall in love again.

424
00:33:19,106 --> 00:33:24,106
生まれては消えてゆくこと
Being born and fading away,

425
00:33:24,106 --> 00:33:28,106
それだけを繰り返している
that is all we keep repeating.

426
00:33:28,106 --> 00:33:34,606
そして君も夜の海に帰ってゆくんだろう
And you too will probably return to the night sea.

427
00:33:34,606 --> 00:33:39,106
生まれては消えてゆくだけの
Just being born and fading away,

428
00:33:39,106 --> 00:33:44,606
青ずんだ波に名前をつけることに
by giving names to these blue-bruised waves,

429
00:33:44,606 --> 00:33:48,606
囚われている項目
we are trapped.

430
00:33:48,606 --> 00:33:53,606
覚えているかな
I wonder if you remember,

431
00:33:53,606 --> 00:33:57,606
いつかの春の朝に
on that spring morning,

432
00:33:57,606 --> 00:34:05,606
桜の木の下で 約束したこと
the promise we made under the cherry blossom tree.

433
00:34:05,606 --> 00:34:11,106
思い出も君の名前も
Even memories and your name,

434
00:34:11,106 --> 00:34:15,606
いつの日か失ってしまって
will someday be lost,

435
00:34:15,606 --> 00:34:21,606
僕もいつかこの海と一つになるんだろう
and I too will eventually become one with this sea.

436
00:34:21,606 --> 00:34:25,606
君のいない冬の空気が
The winter air without you,

437
00:34:25,606 --> 00:34:29,606
僕の頬を刺すその痛みさえ
stings my cheeks, and even that pain,

438
00:34:29,606 --> 00:34:35,106
愛していたい
I want to cherish.

439
00:34:35,106 --> 00:34:39,606
生まれては消えてゆくこと
Being born and fading away,

440
00:34:39,606 --> 00:34:43,606
それだけを繰り返している
that is all we keep repeating.

441
00:34:43,606 --> 00:34:50,106
僕らがもし また会えたらなんて 思ってた
I wondered if we could ever meet again.

442
00:34:50,106 --> 00:34:54,606
生まれては消えてゆくだけの
Just being born and fading away,

443
00:34:54,606 --> 00:35:00,106
青ずんだ波に名前をつけることに
did it make any sense to give names to these blue-bruised waves,

444
00:35:00,106 --> 00:35:01,506
意味はなかったのかななんてさ
or was there no meaning after all?

445
00:35:39,390 --> 00:35:40,390
unhappy?

446
00:35:40,390 --> 00:35:41,390
悩める人の子よ
You troubled child of man,

447
00:35:41,390 --> 00:35:42,090
unlucky?

448
00:35:42,090 --> 00:35:43,390
人ならざる者も
And even those who are not human,

449
00:35:43,390 --> 00:35:44,090
be happy!

450
00:35:44,090 --> 00:35:44,890
弛まず目指せよ
Keep aiming for it without rest,

451
00:35:44,890 --> 00:35:46,090
生きているんだし
after all, you are alive.

452
00:35:46,090 --> 00:35:47,890
目を逸らした過去も
The past you turned your eyes from,

453
00:35:47,890 --> 00:35:49,390
退屈な未来も
and the boring future too.

454
00:35:49,390 --> 00:35:51,290
カウンセリング やれやれ
Counseling, good grief.

455
00:35:51,290 --> 00:35:52,890
古今東西 ピースピース
All times and places, peace, peace!

456
00:35:52,890 --> 00:35:53,790
unhappy?

457
00:35:54,490 --> 00:35:55,590
unlucky?

458
00:35:56,290 --> 00:35:57,390
be happy!

459
00:35:57,890 --> 00:35:59,190
undead

460
00:36:05,590 --> 00:36:06,690
ねえねえねえねえ
Hey, hey, hey, hey,

461
00:36:06,690 --> 00:36:09,990
何だかどうして 戦ってるようなそんな気がするの
somehow, for some reason, I feel like I'm fighting.

462
00:36:09,990 --> 00:36:11,190
触れられない 触れたくもない
Can't touch it, don't even want to touch it,

463
00:36:11,190 --> 00:36:13,090
過去の自分自分自分自分と
my past self, self, self, self...

464
00:36:13,090 --> 00:36:15,990
もうとっくに死んでる透明な亡霊と対決
Confronting a transparent ghost that's already long dead.

465
00:36:15,990 --> 00:36:19,190
幼気で痛い記憶の奥
Deep within childhood's painful memories,

466
00:36:19,190 --> 00:36:20,490
残念 もう居ないのに
what a shame, even though they're no longer here.

467
00:36:20,490 --> 00:36:22,590
あれ そっちが良い？アイロニーね
Oh? Is that one better? How ironic.

468
00:36:22,590 --> 00:36:25,990
透かされてるのは現在の自分？ナンセンス
Is it my current self being seen through? Nonsense.

469
00:36:25,990 --> 00:36:28,090
消えないレッテル
An indelible label.

470
00:36:28,090 --> 00:36:29,490
yes!要はコンプレックス
Yes! In short, a complex.

471
00:36:29,490 --> 00:36:31,390
取り憑かれてるみたい
It's like I'm possessed,

472
00:36:31,390 --> 00:36:33,090
巻き付いたまま
tightly wrapped around me,

473
00:36:33,090 --> 00:36:35,790
まだ離れない 在りし日の自分
and still not letting go—my past self.

474
00:36:38,790 --> 00:36:39,790
undead

475
00:36:39,790 --> 00:36:42,390
死んじゃない お前とお前の連鎖
I'm not dead, the chain of you and yourself.

476
00:36:42,390 --> 00:36:46,390
生きていることとは変わり続けることだ
To live is to keep on changing.

477
00:36:46,390 --> 00:36:49,590
不幸に甘んじて満足するなよ
Don't settle for unhappiness and be satisfied.

478
00:36:49,590 --> 00:36:53,190
幸せになろうとしないなんて卑怯だ
Not even trying to be happy is cowardly.

479
00:36:53,190 --> 00:36:56,190
この世この世は奇怪奇怪ファンタジー
This world is a bizarre, bizarre fantasy.

480
00:36:56,190 --> 00:36:59,190
次は鬼が出るか蛇が出るか
Will a demon or a snake appear next?

481
00:36:59,190 --> 00:37:02,390
出会って遭ってやっと始まる物語
Meeting and encountering, the story finally begins.

482
00:37:02,390 --> 00:37:04,390
さあ人か化物か
Now, is it a human or a monster?

483
00:37:04,390 --> 00:37:06,190
閑話休題 ピースピース
But back to the point, peace, peace!

484
00:37:06,190 --> 00:37:07,890
past & future

485
00:37:07,890 --> 00:37:09,790
can't change the past

486
00:37:09,790 --> 00:37:11,590
past & future

487
00:37:11,590 --> 00:37:13,390
run for the future

488
00:37:13,390 --> 00:37:13,890
カットイン
Cut-in!

489
00:37:13,890 --> 00:37:17,090
何だかどうして未来になんぞ何の希望もない期待出来ない
Somehow, for some reason, there's no hope, no expectation for the future...

490
00:37:17,090 --> 00:37:19,590
ような気がして
That's how I feel.

491
00:37:19,590 --> 00:37:22,590
もう随分生きている既視感とテンプレで食傷
I've lived long enough to be sick of clichés and déjà vu.

492
00:37:22,590 --> 00:37:25,590
素敵な出来事の気配もない
There's no sign of anything wonderful.

493
00:37:25,790 --> 00:37:26,590
残念
What a shame.

494
00:37:26,590 --> 00:37:29,390
積んだ経験の因果形骸化された神話と退屈な進化
The karma of experience: hollowed myths and boring evolution.

495
00:37:29,390 --> 00:37:31,390
要は刺激が欲しいんだ
In short, I just want some excitement.

496
00:37:31,390 --> 00:37:32,990
飽きちゃった 慣れちゃった
I'm bored of it, I've got used to it,

497
00:37:32,990 --> 00:37:34,590
なんて
or so I say.

498
